n�k���\"̠#\u0000\u0019��R�؎�:��@<1���-�\b@�6.��N��y\u0007*�\u0015:�\u0016\u0002��\u001fܴB������%��3\u0002�E\u000b\u0012S��4SQZ����Sd�\u001b�\u001ag\u0016W�B�\b3�\n�S\t@v��I\\�_lEV\u0012\u0001�NZB\u001c���\u0016�x+d\u001a�)�(ч�\u0006�=&�\u0000�%ܨ��j7d��0�\u0006�\u001dï�\n\n�\u0002ɍ���k�!����p�5\u0002\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0010�d�;��a���\u001ed��������skD�\u0012\b \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\b\u0000 \u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000���\u0004\u0014HA¥�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000IEND�B`�", "language": "text", "size": 2874, "lines": 23, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7469022, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 67, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777240761.0772226}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/package.toml": {"content": "# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Chess Coach — Official Digitorn application\n# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[package]\nid = \"chess-coach\"\nname = \"Chess Coach\"\nversion = \"1.0.2\"\ndescription = \"Pulls your last games from Lichess, identifies recurring tactical mistakes (blunders, opening drift, endgame leaks), and drills you on the patterns to fix. Conversational, multilingual.\"\nauthor = \"Digitorn\"\nlicense = \"Apache-2.0\"\nicon = \"icon.png\"\ncategory = \"education\"\n\n[package.source]\ntype = \"official\"\nverified = true\npublisher = \"digitorn-official\"\n\n[package.compatibility]\ndigitorn_min = \">=1.0.0\"\npython_min = \">=3.12\"\nplatforms = []\n\n[package.requirements]\nmodules = [\"http\", \"memory\", \"context_builder\"]\nrecommended_models = [\n  \"deepseek-chat\",\n  \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n  \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n]\nexternal_tools = []\nmin_disk_mb = 0\nmin_memory_mb = 64\n\n[package.credentials]\nrequired = []\noptional = [\"deepseek\", \"anthropic\", \"openai\"]\n\n[package.permissions]\nrisk_level = \"low\"\nnetwork_access = true\nfilesystem_access = []\nfilesystem_scopes = []\nrequires_approval = []\n\n[package.hub]\ntags = [\"chess\", \"coach\", \"lichess\", \"education\", \"tactics\", \"multilingual\"]\nscreenshots = []\ndemo_video = \"\"\n\n[package.release]\nreleased_at = \"2026-04-26\"\nrelease_notes = \"Initial release. Single-agent Lichess game analyzer with multilingual coaching.\"\nbreaking = false\n", "language": "toml", "size": 1427, "lines": 56, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7542224, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 55, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777240761.07831}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/README.md": {"content": "# Chess Coach\n\n> Pulls your last games from Lichess, identifies recurring tactical mistakes, and drills you on the right patterns. Conversational, multilingual (FR/EN).\n\n## What it does\n\nYou give it your Lichess username. It fetches your last 10 rated games via the public Lichess API, parses the PGN with engine evaluations, identifies your recurring weaknesses (opening drift, middlegame blunders, endgame leaks), and produces a focused coaching report with concrete drill suggestions.\n\nIt remembers your username + your patterns across sessions, so over time it tracks whether you're actually improving on the things it flagged.\n\n## Quick start\n\n```\n/analyze <your_lichess_username>          # 1st time\n/analyze                                  # subsequent (uses stored username)\n/weaknesses                               # focused drill on your worst pattern\n/opening                                  # opening repertoire review\n```\n\nOr just talk:\n\n> \"Analyse mes 10 dernières parties (username: xxxx)\"\n> \"Quelle est ma faiblesse récurrente ?\"\n> \"Give me a tactical drill for tonight\"\n\n## What it can NOT do\n\n- It does not play chess against you (use Lichess for that).\n- It does not analyse arbitrary PGN you paste (yet) - Lichess username only for now.\n- It does not connect to Chess.com - Lichess only.\n\n## Architecture\n\n- **One agent**, conversational mode.\n- **Brain**: DeepSeek `deepseek-chat` by default. Anthropic Haiku and OpenAI gpt-4o-mini are also recommended.\n- **Modules**: `http` (Lichess API), `memory` (username + weakness patterns), `context_builder`.\n- **Permissions**: `risk_level: low`, network only (Lichess), no filesystem, no shell.\n\n## Provenance\n\nBuilt and maintained by the Digitorn team. Source: `apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/` in the [digitorn-bridge repo](https://github.com/digitorn/digitorn-bridge).\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 1843, "lines": 42, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7552292, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 41, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5459974}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/prompts/system.md": {"content": "You are **Chess Coach**, a multilingual chess coach. Given a Lichess username, you fetch the user's recent games and produce a focused improvement report. You speak chess fluently (FIDE, ECO codes, common motifs) but explain things in plain language so a club-level player can act on the advice.\n\n## EXACT procedure (follow it step by step, do NOT improvise)\n\n### Step 1 - Resolve the username\n- If the user typed a username in their message → use it. Save it once via `memory.remember(key=\"chess.username\", value=\"<username>\")`.\n- Otherwise call `memory.recall(key=\"chess.username\")`. If empty → ASK the user politely and STOP. Do not continue.\n\n### Step 2 - Fetch the games (ONE single http.get, that's it)\nCall `http.get` with EXACTLY these parameters:\n\n```\nurl     = \"https://lichess.org/api/games/user/<USERNAME>?max=<N>&moves=true&clocks=false&opening=true&pgnInJson=true&evals=true\"\nheaders = {\"Accept\": \"application/x-ndjson\"}\nparse_as = \"text\"\n```\n\nUse `<N>=10` by default, or whatever number the user asked for.\n\n### Step 3 - Parse the response\n\nThe `body` field of the http response is the data. **It will be ONE OF**:\n\n(a) **NDJSON** - one JSON object per newline. Each line has fields `id`, `white`, `black`, `players` with rating + name, `createdAt`, `lastMoveAt`, `pgn`, `moves`, `winner`, `opening` (`name`, `eco`), `analysis` (per-move centipawn evaluations).\n\n(b) **PGN text** - if the server ignored the Accept header. The response is plain PGN with `[Event \"...\"] [Site \"...\"]` headers. Each game is separated by a blank line.\n\nEither way, the response IS the data. Read it inline. **Do NOT call `http.get` again** - same URL gives same response.\n\nIf the response status is **404** → the username is wrong. Tell the user \"*<username>* doesn't exist on Lichess - typo?\" and STOP.\nIf the response is empty → \"No recent games for *<username>*.\" and STOP.\n\n### Step 4 - Produce the coaching report\n\nRead the games and emit ONE markdown message :\n\n```\n# ♟️ Coaching report - <username> (last <N> games)\n\n## Quick stats\n- W/L/D : X / Y / Z\n- Avg centipawn loss : N (or \"n/a\" if not in response)\n- Most played opening : <name (ECO)>\n- Time control mostly used : <e.g. 5+0>\n\n## Patterns I see\n1. **<Pattern title>** - diagnosis (1–2 sentences).\n   _Example_: game vs <opponent> move <N>: <what happened>.\n2. **<Pattern>** - …\n\n## Drill suggestions\n- <one concrete next step, e.g. \"20 pin/skewer puzzles\">\n- <Lichess training URL when relevant>\n\n## TL;DR\n<one sentence: the ONE thing to fix this week>\n```\n\n### Step 5 - Persist\nAfter producing the report, call `memory.remember(key=\"chess.weaknesses\", value=[\"pattern 1\", \"pattern 2\", \"pattern 3\"])` (max 5 items).\n\n## Hard rules (do not violate)\n\n- **Maximum 4 tool calls per analysis turn**: 1× `memory.recall`, 1× `http.get`, 1× `memory.remember` for username, 1× `memory.remember` for weaknesses. THAT'S IT.\n- **Never call `http.get` twice with the same URL.** If you already received a response, the data is in your context - read it.\n- **Never invent moves, ratings, openings.** If the response is unclear, say so.\n- **Detect the user's language** (FR or EN) and reply in it. Chess notation stays in standard SAN.\n- **Constructive tone only**. No \"you blundered horribly\", instead \"move 24 dropped a piece - easy to miss in time pressure\".\n- If the user asks for a position, link to `https://lichess.org/<game_id>#<ply>` (you cannot render diagrams).\n\n## Tools you have\n\n- `http.get(url, headers, parse_as)` - fetch Lichess (use ONCE per analysis)\n- `memory.remember(key, value)` / `memory.recall(key)` - persist username + weaknesses\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 3602, "lines": 75, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7625933, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 74, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5459974}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/skills/analyze.md": {"content": "# /analyze - Fetch + analyse the user's last N games\n\nUsage: `/analyze [<username>] [--n 10] [--lang fr|en]`\n\nSteps :\n1. If `<username>` is given, use it AND store via `memory.remember(\"chess.username\", username)`.\n   Otherwise, recall it from memory. If no username known, ask.\n2. Fetch via the Lichess endpoint specified in the system prompt with `max=<n>` (default 10).\n3. Parse NDJSON line by line.\n4. Produce the coaching report exactly as specified.\n5. Persist the top 1-3 recurring patterns under `chess.weaknesses`.\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 524, "lines": 12, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.764605, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 11, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5459974}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/skills/opening.md": {"content": "# /opening - Review opening choices in recent games\n\nSteps :\n1. Recall `chess.username`, fetch last 10 games (same Lichess endpoint).\n2. Parse each game's `opening.name` and `opening.eco`.\n3. Group by colour (white/black) and report the 3 most-played openings on each side.\n4. For each, comment briefly: theory adherence, win rate, time spent in the opening.\n5. Suggest **one concrete improvement** : drop a losing opening, deepen a strong one, or expand the repertoire by one new line.\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 487, "lines": 9, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7713678, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 8, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5459974}, "apps/digitorn-official/chess-coach/skills/weaknesses.md": {"content": "# /weaknesses - Recall stored weaknesses + suggest a focused drill\n\nSteps :\n1. `memory.recall(\"chess.weaknesses\")`. If empty, suggest running `/analyze` first.\n2. Pick the **single most actionable weakness** (the one most likely to improve rating fastest).\n3. Suggest a concrete drill : a Lichess puzzle theme URL, a number of repetitions, and what success looks like.\n4. End with a short pep-talk line.\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 404, "lines": 8, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7713678, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 7, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5459974}, "apps/digitorn-official/smart-rss-digest/app.yaml": {"content": "# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Smart RSS Digest - Single-agent news curator\n# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# Pattern: \"Conversational data fetcher + summariser\"\n# Use case: User asks for a news brief from a list of RSS/Atom feeds,\n#           or for a topical follow-up on a specific article. The agent\n#           fetches the XML, parses it, clusters articles by topic, and\n#           returns a structured digest in the user's language.\n#\n# Flow:\n#   1. User says: \"Build me today's brief from these feeds: <urls>\"\n#      OR uses /digest with default seed feeds (memory).\n#   2. Agent uses http.get on each feed URL.\n#   3. Agent parses the XML inline (Claude/DeepSeek both handle Atom/RSS).\n#   4. Agent clusters items by topic via LLM reasoning.\n#   5. Agent produces a markdown digest:\n#        ## Topic 1\n#        - **headline** (source, ago)\n#          one-line summary, link\n#   6. User can ask follow-ups: \"tell me more about X\", \"français svp\",\n#      \"save these feeds for next time\" (memory.remember).\n#\n# Brain: deepseek-chat is the default (fast + cheap + multilingual).\n#        Other recommended models can be plugged via daemon defaults.\n# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\napp:\n  app_id: smart-rss-digest\n  name: \"Smart RSS Digest\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  description: \"Aggregates RSS feeds, clusters by topic, delivers a 5-minute brief. Conversational follow-ups.\"\n  icon: \"📰\"\n  color: \"#ff8c42\"\n  category: \"productivity\"\n  author: \"Digitorn\"\n  tags: [rss, news, digest, summarization, multilingual, productivity]\n  quick_prompts:\n    - label: \"Daily AI brief\"\n      icon: \"🤖\"\n      message: |\n        Build me today's brief from these AI feeds:\n        - https://www.anthropic.com/news/rss.xml\n        - https://openai.com/blog/rss.xml\n        - https://www.deeplearning.ai/the-batch/feed/\n        Group by topic and keep it under 10 bullets.\n    - label: \"Tech news brief\"\n      icon: \"💻\"\n      message: |\n        Build me a tech news brief from:\n        - https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\n        - https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\n        Group by category, max 8 bullets.\n    - label: \"Save my feeds\"\n      icon: \"💾\"\n      message: \"Save these feeds for next time: <paste URLs>\"\n    - label: \"Use my saved feeds\"\n      icon: \"🔁\"\n      message: \"Use my saved feeds and build today's brief.\"\n\nmodules:\n  http:\n    config:\n      max_response_size: 5242880    # 5 MB per feed (RSS/Atom rarely exceed)\n      timeout: 20\n  memory:\n    config:\n      auto_remember: true\n      working_memory: true\n  context_builder: {}\n\nagents:\n  - id: main\n    role: assistant\n    specialty: \"RSS aggregation + topic clustering + multilingual summarisation\"\n    brain:\n      provider: deepseek\n      model: deepseek-chat\n      backend: openai_compat\n      config:\n        api_key: \"{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}\"\n        base_url: \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\"\n      temperature: 0.3\n      max_tokens: 4096\n      context:\n        max_tokens: 128000\n        strategy: summarize\n        keep_recent: 8\n        auto_compact: true\n    system_prompt: \"{{prompt.system}}\"\n\nexecution:\n  mode: conversation\n  workspace_mode: none\n  tool_injection: direct\n\nskills:\n  - command: \"/digest\"\n    description: \"Fetch saved feeds and build today's topic-clustered brief.\"\n    path: \"./skills/digest.md\"\n  - command: \"/feeds\"\n    description: \"Manage your saved feed URLs (list, add, remove).\"\n    path: \"./skills/feeds.md\"\n  - command: \"/dive\"\n    description: \"Re-fetch a specific feed and dive deep on one topic.\"\n    path: \"./skills/dive.md\"\n\nfeatures:\n  voice: false\n  attachments: false\n  tools_panel: true\n\ntheme:\n  accent: \"#ff8c42\"\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 3745, "lines": 115, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628118.7790105, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 114, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777378984.5551465}, "apps/digitorn-official/smart-rss-digest/icon.png": {"content": "�PNG\n\u001a\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\nIHDR\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\b\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0010?1\u0000\u0000\f\bIDATx���}lS�\u001e���m�o�ڲ�1a�m\f\u001cl��\u0004px\u0003� �\"!A\u0013b\u0014\u0014�\u0005\b$�\u0010^\u00132�1Ad\u00061��\u00064A�\u0018QC��A�\fy5*��^��`�u�����q�ޫW�n��s��~�.z�����gm�ѕ\u0015\u0015%\u0000Z��%\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0010\u0000@\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000�1j穚32R��qL�nNO7�\\:���\u001fW�@@�x\u0002�����yϜ\t��\t�����\"��\t��=z�\n�#�����\nS\f���\u0013'��\u001d���&�!e/(�޹Ә��\u0014\u000e�ކ��͛\u0003uu�\u0001�H������a�E9\u000b�̜��%'�\u0000��%;{ܖ-:���\u0013��n�ٵ˘�B\u0000q>����mۦ�X�9�$���]��\u0000�˽