rocess | ✅ | 0.37s |  |\n| `QUE03` | queue: cancel endpoint cancels queued (not running) message | ✅ | 0.96s |  |\n| `QUE04` | queue: rehydrate_on_boot resets stuck running rows to queued | ✅ | 0.04s |  |\n| `QUE05` | session config has queue block with default_mode='async' | ✅ | 0.00s |  |\n| `QUE06` | merge_or_enqueue folds rapid consecutive messages into one row | ✅ | 0.08s |  |\n| `QUE07` | replace_last_or_enqueue swaps the tail queued message in place | ✅ | 0.07s |  |\n| `EVT01` | every non-ephemeral event is persisted in session_events table | ✅ | 0.28s |  |\n| `EVT03` | join_session replay reads from DB (async_replay), survives daemon restart | ✅ | 0.07s |  |\n| `EVT04` | seq stays monotonic across daemon restart (DB-seeded) | ✅ | 0.06s |  |\n| `EVT05` | assistant_stream_snapshot is non-ephemeral → persisted for mid-turn reconnect | ✅ | 0.00s |  |\n| `EVT02` | GET /events returns persisted log ordered by seq with filter | ✅ | 2.04s |  |\n| `ORD01` | event_buffer.next_seq is strictly monotonic per user | ✅ | 0.02s |  |\n| `ORD02` | user_replay returns events in seq order with since filter | ✅ | 0.01s |  |\n| `QUE10` | manager.drain_session_queue method exists on AppManager | ✅ | 0.13s |  |\n| `QUE09` | join_session emits queue:snapshot with entries + is_active + running_correlation_id | ✅ | 0.06s |  |\n| `QUE08` | mark_done/failed does NOT overwrite a row already in terminal state | ✅ | 0.04s |  |\n| `CON01` | session lock timeout classified as session_busy (not a generic crash) | ✅ | 0.72s |  |\n| `CON02` | session.lock_timeout config defaults to 600s, within 5-3600s bounds | ✅ | 0.00s |  |\n| `WSP22` | full state round-trip: files+diagnostics+validation+baselines+stats survive reopen | ✅ | 2.91s |  |\n| `WSP20` | filesystem.write also publishes diagnostics + inline lint | ✅ | 12.29s |  |\n| `LSP02` | POST /lsp/request returns 400 when extension has no server | ✅ | 9.88s |  |\n| `LSP03` | POST /lsp/request returns 404 when app has no LSP module | ✅ | 0.94s | 