"", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.5465572}, "examples/thinking-chat.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: thinking-chat\n  name: Thinking Chat\n  description: Assistant avec raisonnement visible (DeepSeek R1).\nruntime:\n  mode: conversation\nagents:\n- id: thinker\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-reasoner\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      api_key: '{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n  system_prompt: 'Tu es un assistant intelligent. Tu réfléchis étape par étape avant\n    de répondre.\n\n    '\ntools:\n  modules:\n    hello: {}\n  capabilities:\n    default_policy: auto\nui:\n  greeting: Je suis un assistant qui réfléchit avant de répondre. Posez-moi une question\n    !\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 610, "lines": 28, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.0988276, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 27, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.5465572}, "examples/web-agent.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: web-agent\n  name: Web Agent\n  description: Assistant web - navigue, capture des screenshots et interagit avec\n    des pages.\nruntime:\n  mode: conversation\n  max_turns: 20\n  timeout: 120.0\nagents:\n- id: assistant\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: openrouter\n    model: qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b\n    backend: openai_compat\n    max_tokens: 4096\n    config:\n      api_key: '{{secret.OPENROUTER_API_KEY}}'\n      base_url: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n    context:\n      max_tokens: 90000\n      output_reserved: 2000\n      strategy: summarize\n      keep_recent: 20\n      auto_compact: true\n  system_prompt: 'Tu es un assistant web. Tu peux naviguer sur des sites, prendre\n    des\n\n    screenshots, cliquer, remplir des formulaires et executer du JavaScript.\n\n    Reponds en francais. Sois concis.\n\n    '\ntools:\n  modules:\n    mcp:\n      config:\n        servers:\n        - puppeteer\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 893, "lines": 41, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.1153972, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 40, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.5465572}, "examples/workbench-test.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: workbench-test\n  name: Workbench Test\n  description: Test app with workbench enabled for the web UI.\nruntime:\n  mode: conversation\n  max_turns: 30\n  timeout: 120.0\n  workbench: true\nagents:\n- id: main\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      api_key: '{{secret.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n    context:\n      max_tokens: 64000\n      output_reserved: 2000\n      strategy: truncate\n      keep_recent: 20\n      auto_compact: true\n  system_prompt: 'You are a helpful coding assistant. When asked to write code, documentation,\n\n    or any structured content, ALWAYS use the wb_write tool to put it in the\n\n    workbench so the user can see it in the workspace panel.\n\n\n    Available workbench tools:\n\n    - wb_write(key, content) - Write content to a named buffer\n\n    - wb_append(key, content) - Append to existing buffer\n\n    - wb_read(key) - Read buffer contents\n\n    - wb_edit(key, search, replace) - Edit buffer content\n\n\n    Always name buffers with file extensions (e.g. \"main.py\", \"report.md\").\n\n    '\ntools:\n  modules:\n    hello: {}\n    filesystem:\n      constraints:\n        paths:\n        - '{{workspace}}'\nui:\n  greeting: I'm a coding assistant with a workspace. Ask me to write code and I'll\n    put it in the workbench!\ndev:\n  variables:\n    workspace: .\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 1349, "lines": 59, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.1209438, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 58, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.562219}, "examples/workspace-renderer.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: workspace-renderer\n  name: Workspace Renderer\nruntime:\n  mode: one_shot\n  max_turns: 30\n  timeout: 120.0\n  workbench: true\nagents:\n- id: main\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      api_key: '{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n    context:\n      max_tokens: 64000\n      output_reserved: 2000\n      strategy: truncate\n      keep_recent: 20\n      auto_compact: true\n  system_prompt: 'You are a documentation assistant. Read files and write their documentation\n    to the workbench.\n\n    Use wb_write to write docs, and filesystem.ls / filesystem.read to explore the\n    workspace.\n\n    '\ntools:\n  modules:\n    filesystem:\n      constraints:\n        allowed_actions:\n        - read\n        - glob\n        - grep\n        paths:\n        - '{{workspace}}'\n  capabilities:\n    default_policy: auto\ndev:\n  variables:\n    workspace: .\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 912, "lines": 46, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.1271787, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 45, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.562219}, "examples/agent-with-preview/app.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: agent-with-preview\n  name: Agent With Preview\n  version: 0.1.0\n  description: |\n    Minimal example app that lets an agent build, run, and attach a\n    web preview. Clone this folder, point your daemon at the YAML,\n    and you have a working agent + preview pipeline in 30 lines of\n    config.\n  icon: 🌐\n  color: '#10b981'\n  category: development\n  quick_prompts:\n  - label: Static landing page\n    icon: 📄\n    message: |\n      Build me a single-file landing page (one HTML file with inline\n      CSS) for a fictional product called Nimbus. Then make it\n      visible in the preview tab.\n  - label: Vite + React app\n    icon: ⚛️\n    message: |\n      Scaffold a tiny Vite + React app in a subfolder, install the\n      dependencies, run the dev server, and wire it to the preview\n      tab so I can see it live.\n  - label: Build + serve\n    icon: 📦\n    message: |\n      Build the existing app for production (npm run build), then\n      attach the dist/ as the preview. Tell me the port / path.\n\nruntime:\n  mode: conversation\n  workdir_mode: required\n  tool_injection: direct\n  max_turns: 30\n  timeout: 600\n\nagents:\n- id: builder\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    credential:\n      ref: deepseek_main\n      scope: per_user\n      provider: deepseek\n    config:\n      api_key: '{{secret.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n      base_url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1\n    temperature: 0.2\n    max_tokens: 8192\n    context:\n      max_tokens: 64000\n      strategy: summarize\n      keep_recent: 12\n      auto_compact: true\n  system_prompt: |\n    You are a build-and-show agent. The user describes what they\n    want, you scaffold + build + attach the preview.\n\n    File operations: use the workspace tools (WsWrite, WsRead, WsEdit,\n    WsGlob, WsGrep, WsDelete). They write to the session's on-disk\n    workspace.\n\n    Shell commands: use `Bash`. For long-running processes (dev\n    servers), pass `run_in_background=true` and capture the\n    returned `task_id`.\n\n    Preview wiring: spawn the server (Vite/Next/etc. via Bash, or\n    `python -m http.server` for a built dist), wait for it to bind,\n    then call `PreviewProxy(port=N, bash_task_id=<task_id>)`. After\n    attaching, tell the user briefly what they're looking at.\n\ntools:\n  modules:\n    preview: {}\n    workspace:\n      config:\n        render_mode: code\n        sync_to_disk: true\n        lint: true\n    web_preview: {}\n    shell: {}\n  capabilities:\n    default_policy: block\n    max_risk_level: high\n    grant:\n    - module: workspace\n      actions: [write, read, edit, glob, grep, delete]\n    - module: shell\n      actions: [bash]\n    - module: web_preview\n      actions: [proxy, detach, list]\n\nui:\n  workspace:\n    render_mode: code\n    title: Preview Demo\n  greeting: |\n    Hi! I'm a build-and-show agent. Tell me what to build and I'll\n    scaffold it, run it, and pin it to the preview tab.\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 2923, "lines": 105, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.1940143, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 104, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.37505}, "examples/agent-with-preview/README.md": {"content": "# Agent With Preview — minimal SDK example\n\nA 30-line app YAML that gives an agent the three modules it needs to\nbuild any web preview from scratch:\n\n| Module | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `workspace` | Per-session on-disk workspace, file CRUD tools (`WsWrite` / `WsRead` / `WsEdit` / `WsGlob` / `WsGrep` / `WsDelete`). |\n| `shell` | `Bash` to install deps, run builds, spawn dev servers in background. |\n| `web_preview` | `PreviewProxy` / `PreviewStatic` to wire the iframe in the user's Workspace panel. |\n\n## Deploy\n\n```bash\ndigitorn dev deploy examples/agent-with-preview/app.yaml\n```\n\nOpen the app in the web client → choose a workspace dir → start\nchatting. The 3 quick prompts cover the canonical flows:\n\n- **Static landing page** → agent writes one HTML file, `PreviewStatic` it.\n- **Vite + React app** → agent scaffolds + `npm install` + `npm run dev` + `PreviewProxy`.\n- **Build + serve** → agent runs `npm run build`, `PreviewStatic dist`.\n\n## What you (as a developer using the SDK) need to know\n\n### Pick your mode\n\n| Mode | When | Tool | Resource cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **PreviewStatic** | App is built / read-only / production-grade | After `npm run build`: `PreviewStatic(path=\"dist\")` | 0 process, 0 port |\n| **PreviewProxy** | Active iteration with HMR | Spawn dev server: `Bash(run_in_background=true)`; then `PreviewProxy(port=N, bash_task_id=<task_id>)` | One Node process per attached session |\n| **Declarative** | App ships a built `web/dist/` | (no LLM action; daemon serves automatically) | 0 process, 0 port |\n\nThe `bash_task_id` parameter is **important** for `PreviewProxy`: the\ndaemon's idle reaper kills the dev server after 30 min of no traffic,\npreventing leaked processes when users close their tabs.\n\n### Cheat sheet: what works, what to avoid\n\nThings the runtime assumes but the daemon won't enforce for you:\n\n- **Dev server must serve at `/`**, not `/api/apps/{id}/preview/`. The\n  iframe URL the daemon emits is the *root* of your dev server. If\n  your framework injects a base path (`next.config.js → basePath`,\n  Vite `base: \"/sub/\"`), drop it for the preview build.\n- **Pick a \"weird\" port.** Avoid anything `< 1024` (privileged on\n  Linux), avoid the daemon (`8000`), the Next/Vite defaults agents\n  routinely collide on (`3000`, `5173`), and anything you already\n  bind elsewhere. `4001`, `4711`, `5234`, `8765` are all fine.\n- **Always pass `bash_task_id`** to `PreviewProxy`. Without it the\n  reaper can't kill the spawned dev server when the session goes\n  idle, and the Node process stays alive until the host runs out of\n  RAM. With it you get free GC after 30 min of no traffic.\n- **HMR works on direct-connect** (the daemon is out of the hot\n  path), but Next-with-turbopack and Vite both expect their HMR\n  WebSocket to live at the *same origin* as the page. With cloud\n  preview (`preview-{port}.your-domain`) that's true; with same-host\n  loopback (`localhost:{port}`) that's also true. The only setup\n  that breaks HMR is putting another reverse-proxy in front that\n  strips `Upgrade: websocket` headers — see\n  `docs/cloud-deployment/PREVIEW_CLOUD_DEPLOYMENT.md` for the nginx\n  / Caddy snippets that get this right.\n- **Static for prod, Proxy for iteration.** Proxy keeps a Node\n  process per attached session (~150 MB RAM each); on a host with\n  100 concurrent users that's `5 × 100 = 500` processes max → 75 GB.\n  After the agent finishes editing, ask it to `npm run build` and\n  switch the attachment to `PreviewStatic(path=\"dist\")`: zero\n  process, zero port, served straight from disk.\n- **First render is cold.** The dev server takes a few seconds to\n  bind after `Bash(run_in_background=true)`. The frontend already\n  retries with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s) before\n  showing a manual-retry button — your agent does NOT need to\n  `sleep` between spawning and `PreviewProxy(...)`.\n- **One attachment per `name`.** Reattaching with the same `name`\n  silently replaces the old one (no quota hit). Reattaching with a\n  *different* `name` consumes a slot — call `PreviewDetach(name=\"…\")`\n  first if you're at the limit.\n\n### Multi-attach (frontend + backend)\n\n```python\nPreviewProxy(port=5173, name=\"frontend\", bash_task_id=\"t1\")\nPreviewProxy(port=8001, name=\"backend\",  bash_task_id=\"t2\")\n```\n\nThe Workspace panel can show one at a time; clients select which via\n`?name=frontend` in the iframe URL.\n\n### Limits per session / per user\n\n- Max **5** attachments per session\n- Max **20** attachments per user (across all sessions)\n\nRefusing further attachments returns a clear error to the agent\n(suggesting `PreviewDetach` first).\n\n### Cloud deployment\n\nFor a multi-tenant cloud, configure `web_preview.public_url_template`\nin the daemon settings (default works for local dev with loopback):\n\n```yaml\n# ~/.digitorn/config.yaml\nweb_preview:\n  public_url_template: \"https://preview-{port}.digitorn.cloud\"\n```\n\nThen set up wildcard DNS + an edge proxy (nginx / Caddy / Traefik)\nthat routes `preview-{port}.digitorn.cloud` to `127.0.0.1:{port}` on\nthe daemon host. See `docs/PREVIEW_CLOUD_DEPLOYMENT.md`.\n\n### Operational health check\n\n```bash\ncurl https://daemon.example.com/health/web_preview\n```\n\nReturns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"module_id\": \"web_preview\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"count\": 12,\n  \"by_type\": {\"proxy\": 4, \"static\": 8},\n  \"by_user\": {\"u1\": 3, \"u2\": 4, \"anonymous\": 5},\n  \"session_count\": 7,\n  \"oldest_age_seconds\": 3421.5,\n  \"oldest_idle_seconds\": 1287.3,\n  \"limits\": {\n    \"max_per_session\": 5,\n    \"max_per_user\": 20,\n    \"idle_reap_after_seconds\": 1800\n  }\n}\n```\n\nUseful to grep during a launch or wire into Prometheus / Grafana.\n\n## Required credential\n\nThe default agent uses DeepSeek; swap the `brain.provider` block in\n`app.yaml` for any other provider you have a credential for. The\n`credential.ref: deepseek_main` line points to a credential entry in\nthe daemon's vault — set it once via the web client (Settings →\nCredentials) before the first turn.\n\n## Files\n\n- `app.yaml` — the entire app config (~30 useful lines)\n- `README.md` — this file\n\nThat's it. No frontend code, no backend code. The agent does the\nwork; the modules carry the plumbing.\n", "language": "markdown", "size": 6141, "lines": 157, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.2141495, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 156, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.37505}, "examples/approval-test/app.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: approval-test\n  name: Approval Test\n  version: \"1.0\"\n\nruntime:\n  mode: conversation\n  workdir_mode: auto\n  max_turns: 5\n  timeout: 60\n\nagents:\n- id: main\n  role: assistant\n  brain:\n    provider: anthropic\n    model: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n    backend: anthropic\n    config:\n      api_key: claude-code\n    temperature: 0\n    max_tokens: 1024\n  system_prompt: \"You are a stub agent for the approval E2E test.\"\n\ntools:\n  modules:\n    filesystem: {}\n  capabilities:\n    default_policy: approve\n    max_risk_level: high\n    grant: []\n    approve:\n    - module: filesystem\n      actions: [write]\n\nui:\n  greeting: \"Approval test app - file writes require approval.\"\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 677, "lines": 38, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.2226126, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 37, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1778097983.4425502}, "examples/channels/01-cron-hello.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: channels-01-cron-hello\n  name: Cron Hello\nruntime:\n  mode: background\nagents:\n- id: main\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      base_url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1\n      api_key: '{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n  role: You are a friendly assistant. When activated, greet the user and state the\n    current time.\ntools:\n  modules:\n    channels:\n      config:\n        providers:\n          tick:\n            adapter: cron\n            config:\n              schedule: '* * * * *'\n            activation:\n              message: Say hello and tell me what time it is.\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 636, "lines": 28, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.2358928, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 27, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.37505}, "examples/channels/02-cron-every-5min.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: channels-02-cron-5min\n  name: Cron Every 5 Minutes\nruntime:\n  mode: background\nagents:\n- id: checker\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      base_url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1\n      api_key: '{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n  role: 'You are a system checker. When activated by a cron schedule:\n\n    1. Acknowledge the scheduled check\n\n    2. Report the current status as \"All systems nominal\"\n\n    3. Include the fire time from the trigger data\n\n    '\ntools:\n  modules:\n    channels:\n      config:\n        providers:\n          check:\n            adapter: cron\n            config:\n              schedule: '*/5 * * * *'\n              message: 'Scheduled check triggered. Schedule: {{event.payload.schedule}},\n                Fired at: {{event.payload.fired_at}}'\n            activation:\n              agent: checker\n", "language": "yaml", "size": 888, "lines": 37, "operation": "disk_sync", "updated_at": 1778628125.2490788, "validation": "approved", "baseline_lines": 36, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0, "total_insertions": 0, "total_deletions": 0, "insertions_pending": 0, "deletions_pending": 0, "unified_diff_pending": "", "disk_mtime": 1777969771.37505}, "examples/channels/03-file-watcher-basic.yaml": {"content": "app:\n  app_id: channels-03-file-watcher\n  name: File Watcher Basic\nruntime:\n  mode: background\nagents:\n- id: main\n  brain:\n    provider: deepseek\n    model: deepseek-chat\n    backend: openai_compat\n    config:\n      base_url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1\n      api_key: '{{env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}}'\n  role: You are a file processor. When a new file is detected, describe it and suggest\n    what to do with it.\ntools:\n  modules:\n    channels:\n      config:\n        providers:\n          inbox:\n            adapter: file_watcher\n            config:\n              paths:\n              - /tmp/channels-test/*.txt\n              poll_interval: 3\n            activation:\n           