s registered extensions.\"\n          },\n          \"method\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"title\": \"Method\",\n            \"description\": \"LSP method name (e.g. 'textDocument/hover').\"\n          },\n          \"params\": {\n            \"additionalProperties\": true,\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"title\": \"Params\",\n            \"description\": \"Raw LSP request params. ``textDocument.uri`` auto-filled from ``path`` if omitted; everything else is passed through.\"\n          },\n          \"timeout_seconds\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\",\n            \"maximum\": 60.0,\n            \"minimum\": 0.1,\n            \"title\": \"Timeout Seconds\",\n            \"description\": \"Server-side timeout for the RPC call.\",\n            \"default\": 10.0\n          },\n          \"request_id\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"title\": \"Request Id\",\n            \"description\": \"Client correlation id \\u2014 use it to cancel this specific request later. Daemon mints one if omitted.\"\n          },\n          \"supersede_previous\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\",\n            \"title\": \"Supersede Previous\",\n            \"description\": \"When True, a new request for the same (session, path, method) triple cancels any in-flight request for that triple. Right default for keystroke methods; set False for user-initiated ones (references, rename).\",\n            \"default\": true\n          }\n        },\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"path\",\n          \"method\"\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"LspRpcRequest\",\n        \"description\": \"Body for ``POST /lsp/request``.\\n\\n``method`` + ``params`` follow the Language Server Protocol spec\\n(textDocument/hover, textDocument/definition, textDocument